From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NotAlexNoyle <alexnoyle@icloud.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:43:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] gpu-compositor: a frame without its parts (flag 128) and the
 parts' generation

T-505, the owner's CPU/GPU split ("both, parts first"): the daemon draws a page's fixed and sticky parts
over each frame on the CPU, from a picture of the parts alone, so the GPU composes and reads only the
scrolled content (no fixed rows, keeps or columns for the see-through sidebars).
- flag 128 of jihad_offscreen_compose_post/start: every fixed and every sticky layer (stuck or not) at
  shadow opacity 0 in the composite and in the diff-first step; no fixed rows, keeps or columns; the
  parts' rects still reported with the poll (each part its layer's whole rect, no keeps: the same in a
  frame, where the parts are at opacity 0, and in the parts' picture, flags 64|128, where they are shown;
  the keep split made them differ and the daemon's picture never matched);
- the parts' generation: a count of compositable updates under a fixed or sticky layer, the poll's
  thirtieth int (jihad_offscreen_overview_ok answers 2), so the daemon knows when its picture is old;
- JIHAD_GPU_REQLOG=1 (diagnostic): each composite request's source.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XtfxSpM1w2uiVKeLKoV3g3
